    <node id="Art. 5(1)(c)">
      <data key="d0">Art. 5(1)(c)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Art. 5(1)(c) outlines the principle of data minimization, which mandates that personal data must be adequate, relevant, and limited to what is necessary.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-affbd5dbcf34ebe169fa07a29874fc52</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756582247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Art. 5(1)(e)">
      <data key="d0">Art. 5(1)(e)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Art. 5(1)(e) states the principle of storage limitation, indicating that personal data must not be stored longer than necessary.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-affbd5dbcf34ebe169fa07a29874fc52</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756582247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Art. 6(1)(a)">
      <data key="d0">Art. 6(1)(a)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Art. 6(1)(a) specifies that processing personal data is lawful if the subject has given consent.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-affbd5dbcf34ebe169fa07a29874fc52</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756582247</data>
